msgstr "Senisim Map..."

#: temp.glade:27796 temp.glade:37379
msgid "Switch to the View+Edit tab to\n"
"show/edit the Maps module."
msgstr "Go long View+Edit tab long\n"
"saumi/senisim Maps module."

#: temp.glade:27809
msgid "Show Catalogue..."
msgstr "Soim Katalog..."

#: temp.glade:27813
msgid "Browse the catalogue of commonly\n"
"used Bible illustrations from a range\n"
"of different artists."
msgstr "Lukim katalog bilong ol pikja bilong Baibel\n"
"i save kamap planti taim, bilong ol\n"
"wanwan man i mekim pikja."

#: temp.glade:27861
msgid "The list of pictures can be \n"
"filtered according to the \n"
"status of the checking values."
msgstr "Yu ken filtarim lista bilong ol pikja\n"
"bilong stap long status\n"
"bilong ol chekim velyu."

#: temp.glade:27880
msgid "Exclude Matched"
msgstr "Rausim Ol i Match"

#: temp.glade:27885
msgid "Flip the results of the\n"
"filtered list to exclude\n"
"any items that match."
msgstr "Tanim risal bilong filtarim lista\n"
"bilong rausim olgeta samting\n"
"i match."

#: temp.glade:27907
msgid "Filter Checklist"
msgstr "Filtarim Chekting"

#: temp.glade:27931
msgid "Show Active Books"
msgstr "Soim Ol Buk i Wok"

#: temp.glade:27936
msgid "Select this option to only display the pictures from the\n"
"books that are currently in focus to be printed. \n"
"When unchecked, then the list will show pictures from\n"
"ALL the books in the project that have been added to\n"
"the PicList. If pictures of a certain book are missing, \n"
"then you may need to select that book and Generate\n"
"the PicList details just for *that* book."
msgstr "Makim dispela long soim ol pikja tasol bilong\n"
"ol buk i stap long fokus bilong printim nau.\n"
"Sapos yu no makim, lista bai soim ol pikja bilong\n"
"OLGETA buk long projek we i stap pinis long\n"
"PicList. Sapos ol pikja bilong wanpela buk i lus,\n"
"orait yu mas makim dispela buk na Kamapim\n"
"ol PicList detel bilong *dispela* buk tasol."

#: temp.glade:27964
msgid "Image"
msgstr "Piksa"

#: temp.glade:27969
msgid "Display the picture currently in focus.\n"
"Note that this is dependent on the image\n"
"being located in the specified folder(s)."
msgstr "Soim pikja i stap long fokus nau.\n"
"Tingim, dispela i bilong pikja i mas stap\n"
"long folder o ol folder yu makim."

#: temp.glade:27986
msgid "Position"
msgstr "Ples"

#: temp.glade:27991
msgid "Show the relative position of the picture\n"
"on the page. When Inner/Outer is used,\n"
"the position displayed represents the \n"
"odd/right-hand page of a spread."
msgstr "Soim ples bilong piksa long pes. Taim Insait/Autsait i stap, ples we i soim em ples bilong odd/raithan pes bilong tupela pes i open."

#: temp.glade:28088
msgid "High Resolution\n"
"(Larger File)"
msgstr "Hai Resolusen\n"
"(Bikpela Fail)"

#: temp.glade:28094
msgid "If this option is selected, PTXprint prefers TIF,\n"
"then PNG, then JPG files (and the larger file if\n"
"there are two of the same type).\n"
"\n"
"The original higher-quality illustrations are\n"
"usually larger (.TIF .PNG or .PDF files) and \n"
"are stored in the local\\Figures folder so that\n"
"they are not shared via Send/Recv. If these are\n"
"used, the resulting PDF could be very large, and\n"
"therefore difficult to share electronically, but\n"
"the image quality will be as good as possible."
msgstr "Sapos yu makim dispela opsen, PTXprint i laikim TIF pastaim, bihain PNG, bihain JPG (na bikpela fail sapos tupela i wankain taip).\n"
"\n"
"Ol orijinal piksa i gat gutpela kwaliti save bikpela moa (.TIF .PNG o .PDF fail) na i stap long local\\Figures folder, olsem na ol i no go long Send/Recv. Sapos yu yusim ol, PDF i ken bikpela tumas, na i hat long salim long kompyuta, tasol kwaliti bilong piksa bai i gutpela olgeta."

#: temp.glade:28118
msgid "Low Resolution\n"
"(Smaller File)"
msgstr "Liklik Resolusen\n"
"(Liklik Fail)"

#: temp.glade:28124
msgid "Paratext stores low resolution .JPG versions of\n"
"illustrations in the project's \"Figures\" folder. If\n"
"these are used, the file size of the resulting PDF\n"
"will be relatively small, and therefore easy to\n"
"share, but the image quality will be low."
msgstr "Paratext i save putim ol liklik resolusen .JPG bilong ol piksa long folder \"Figures\" bilong projek. Sapos yu usim ol dispela, fail bilong PDF bai i liklik, na i isi long skelim, tasol kwaliti bilong piksa bai i go daun."

#: temp.glade:28143
msgid "Use Place-holders\n"
"(Smallest PDF File)"
msgstr "Usim Ples Lukautim\n"
"(Liklik PDF Fail Tru)"

#: temp.glade:28149
msgid "Use this option to include an empty box wherever\n"
"illustrations would be placed in the final PDF. \n"
"\n"
"WHY would someone want to do this?\n"
"It is sometimes necessary to generate the smallest\n"
"possible PDF file (usually in order to send by\n"
"e-mail) or to produce a PDF to be printed\n"
"without illustrations."
msgstr "Usim dispela seting long putim wanpela emti bokis long olgeta hap we ol piksa i mas stap long PDF.\n"
"\n"
"HAMAS na bilong wanem wanpela man i laik mekim olsem?\n"
"Sampela taim i gat nid long kamapim liklik PDF fail tru (planti taim bilong salim long i-mel) o long kamapim PDF bilong printim i no gat ol piksa."

#: temp.glade:28173 temp.glade:28174
msgid "Omit Pictures Only Meant for Web or App"
msgstr "Rausim ol Piksa Bilong Web o App Tasol"

#: temp.glade:28178
msgid "Only allow illustrations with the 'P'rint attribute.\n"
"\n"
"If the illustrations have been marked up with\n"
"the w/a/p notation, then it is easy to exclude\n"
"any illustrations that do not have the 'p'\n"
"attribute.  Note: w= web, a=app, p=print."
msgstr "Larim ol piksa i gat 'P'rint atribiut tasol.\n"
"\n"
"Sapos ol piksa i gat mak bilong w/a/p, i isi long rausim ol piksa i no gat 'p' atribiut. Tingim: w= web, a=app, p=print."

#: temp.glade:28198
msgid "How?"
msgstr "Olsem wanem?"

#: temp.glade:28203
msgid "Open a web page that explains how to mark\n"
"pictures in Paratext for print, web or app."
msgstr "Opim wanpela web pes i stori olsem wanem long makim ol piksa long Paratext bilong print, web o app."

#: temp.glade:28229 temp.glade:28230
msgid "Omit Captions "
msgstr "Rausim ol Kapsen "

#: temp.glade:28234
msgid "If you want to suppress the picture\n"
"captions from being displayed below\n"
"the picture, then check this option."
msgstr "Sapos yu no laik soim ol kapsen i stap aninit long piksa, makim dispela seting."

#: temp.glade:28251
msgid "Omit References (ch:vs)"
msgstr "Rausim ol Refrens (kap:ves)"

#: temp.glade:28255
msgid "If you only want to suppress the \n"
"reference part of the caption,\n"
"then check this option. Note that\n"
"it is not possible to just have the\n"
"references without the captions."
msgstr "Sapos yu laik rausim hap refrens tasol bilong kapsen, makim dispela seting. Tingim: i no inap long kisim ol refrens tasol na ol kapsen i no stap."

#: temp.glade:28281
msgid "Omit Missing Pictures ..."
msgstr "Rausim ol Piksa i Lus ..."

#: temp.glade:28286
msgid "Rather than aborting the PDF export process, pre-process\n"
"the list of illustrations and skip/ignore/remove any which\n"
"are not found in the specified location of image files.\n"
"\n"
"If Pictures are missing after preparing a PDF, then\n"
"they will be listed in the section below."
msgstr "Bilong no stopim wok bilong kamapim PDF, PTXprint bai i skelim lista bilong ol piksa pastaim na lusim o rausim ol piksa i no stap long ples bilong ol fail piksa.\n"
"\n"
"Sapos sampela piksa i lus bihain long redim PDF, ol bai i stap long lista aninit."

#: lib/ptxprint/runjob.py:1202
msgid "(0 Missing)"
msgstr "(0 i Lus)"

#: temp.glade:28319
msgid "Remove Image Borders"
msgstr "Rausim ol Border bilong Piksa"

#: temp.glade:28324
msgid "Some images have a thin line on\n"
"one or more of the edges of the\n"
"picture. Enable this option to\n"
"automatically crop these unwanted\n"
"lines from the edge of pictures.\n"
"Note that this setting affects ALL\n"
"images, not just those with lines."
msgstr "Sampela piksa i gat wanpela liklik lain long wanpela o planti sait bilong piksa. Makim dispela seting long katim ol dispela lain yu no laikim long sait bilong ol piksa.\n"
"Tingim: dispela seting i save senisim OLGETA piksa, i no ol piksa i gat lain tasol."

#: temp.glade:28348
msgid "Request Access to High Quality Illustrations/Maps\n"
"in the SIL repository.\n"
"\n"
"Click this button to fill in the form requesting access\n"
"to the illustrations used in the current publication.\n"
"\n"
"After completing and submitting the online form\n"
"you should receive an immediate response by email\n"
"with a link to download the illustrations (if approved)."
msgstr "Askim bilong kisim ol High Quality Piksa/Map long SIL repository.\n"
"\n"
"Klikim dispela boton bilong pulapim fom i askim bilong kisim ol piksa ol i yusim long dispela publikesen.\n"
"\n"
"Bihain long yu pulapim na salim online fom, yu bai kisim kwik ansa long email wantaim wanpela link bilong daunlodim ol piksa (sapos ol i orait)."

#: temp.glade:28369
msgid "Get Permission..."
msgstr "Kisim Pemisen..."

#: temp.glade:28375
msgid "If you are publishing (i.e. more than 50 copies) any\n"
"material with illustrations that require prior permission\n"
"to be obtained before publishing, then click this button\n"
"to automatically fill in the form requesting permission.\n"
"\n"
"Note that any missing information will need to be\n"
"filled in on the Peripherals tab before the form can\n"
"be submitted.\n"
"\n"
"After filling in any remaining details, you will need to\n"
"submit the Google form and wait for a response."
msgstr "Sapos yu pablisim (olsem, moa long 50 kopi) wanpela samting i gat ol piksa we i mas gat pemisen pastaim, klikim dispela boton long pulim fom bilong askim pemisen.\n"
"\n"
"Tingim: sapos sampela infomesen i lus, yu mas pulim long tab Peripherals pastaim bipo yu salim fom.\n"
"\n"
"Bihain long pulim ol narapela samting, yu mas salim Google fom na wetim ansa."

#: temp.glade:28404
msgid "Use Other\n"
"Location: "
msgstr "Usim Narapela\n"
"Ples: "

#: temp.glade:28410
msgid "The following locations are scanned for pictures:\n"
"  My Paratext ... Projects\\<prjID>\\figures\n"
"  My Paratext ... Projects\\<prjID>\\local\\figures\n"
"  Users\\...\\AppData\\Local\\SIL\\ptxprint\\imagesets\n"
"\n"
"If your pictures are in a different folder, then enable\n"
"this option and select a Picture Folder to be scanned\n"
"in addition to the folders listed above. Note that ALL\n"
"subfolders are also scanned unless you explicitly\n"
"enable the 'Exclude Subfolders' option."
msgstr "Ol dispela hap i save painim ol piksa:\n"
"  My Paratext ... Projects\\<prjID>\\figures\n"
"  My Paratext ... Projects\\<prjID>\\local\\figures\n"
"  Users\\...\\AppData\\Local\\SIL\\ptxprint\\imagesets\n"
"\n"
"Sapos ol piksa bilong yu i stap long narapela folder, op dispela opsen na makim wanpela Picture Folder bilong painim wantaim ol folder i stap antap. Save: OLGETA sabfolder i save painim tu sapos yu no op 'Exclude Subfolders' opsen."

#: temp.glade:28433
msgid "Picture Folder..."
msgstr "Folder bilong Piksa..."

#: temp.glade:28439
msgid "Select another folder which contains pictures.\n"
"PTXprint will also scan the selected folder \n"
"(and all its sub-folders) looking for all the\n"
"required illustrations in the Picture List."
msgstr "Makim narapela folder i gat ol piksa. PTXprint bai i painim tu long dispela folder (na olgeta sabfolder bilong en) long painim olgeta piksa i gat nid long Lista bilong Piksa."

#: temp.glade:28473
msgid "Exclude\n"
"Subfolders"
msgstr "Rausim\n"
"Sabfolder"

#: temp.glade:28479
msgid "PTXprint normally searches all the sub-folders of the\n"
"specified folder locations for the pictures it needs.\n"
"\n"
"If you would prefer that it only searches in the folder\n"
"specified directly (and NOT look in any subfolders)\n"
"then select this option. This should speed up searches\n"
"for images, but may result in some images not being\n"
"found at all."
msgstr "PTXprint i save painim olgeta sabfolder bilong ol folder yu makim long painim ol piksa em i nidim.\n"
"\n"
"Sapos yu laik bai em i painim tasol long folder yu makim stret (na NO lukim ol sabfolder), orait makim dispela opsen. Dispela inap mekim painim bilong ol piksa i kwik, tasol sampela piksa i ken no kamap olgeta."

#: temp.glade:28516
msgid "You can specify your preference for which kinds\n"
"of images are used. PTXprint will search multiple\n"
"locations for any matching images, and use the\n"
"one that best matches your preferences (if found).\n"
"\n"
"If the box is left empty, it will default to the \n"
"following search sequences:\n"
"   jpg > png > tif > bmp > pdf   - for smallest file size\n"
"or\n"
"   tif > png > jpg > bmp > pdf   - for largest file size"
msgstr "Yu ken makim wanem kain piksa yu laik yusim. PTXprint bai painim ol piksa long planti ples, na bai yusim dispela i stret moa long laik bilong yu (sapos em i painim).\n"
"\n"
"Sapos yu lusim boks i stap nating, bai em i yusim dispela oda bilong painim:\n"
"   jpg > png > tif > bmp > pdf   - long liklik fail saiz\n"
"o\n"
"   tif > png > jpg > bmp > pdf   - long bikpela fail saiz"

#: temp.glade:28528
msgid "Image Types:"
msgstr "Kain Piksa:"

#: temp.glade:28542
msgid "If multiple versions of an image are located\n"
"(hk12345B.jpg, hk12345C.png or hk12345B.tif)\n"
"then which one of these different image types\n"
"should be used in the publication?\n"
"\n"
"If in doubt, leave this box empty. Then it will\n"
"use one of two defaults:\n"
"\n"
"1. Low Resolution Default Order:\n"
"JPG PNG TIF BMP PDF  (use JPGs first, if none then PNGs, TIFs etc.)\n"
"\n"
"2. High Resolution Default Order:\n"
"TIF PNG JPG BMP PDF (use TIFs first, if none then PNGs, JPGs etc.)\n"
"\n"
"Or manually type in a custom order, for example:\n"
"PDF TIF PNG (use PDFs first, otherwise TIFs, or PNGs)\n"
"  or\n"
"JPG  (only use JPGs - ignore all other file types)\n"
"  or\n"
"TIF  (only use TIFs - ignore all other file types)\n"
"\n"
"NOTE: TIF files are converted internally to hi-res JPGs."
msgstr "Sapos i gat planti piksa bilong wanpela samting (hk12345B.jpg, hk12345C.png o hk12345B.tif), wanem kain piksa bai yusim long buk?\n"
"\n"
"Sapos yu no save, lusim dispela boks i stap nating. Orait bai em i yusim wanpela bilong tupela oda:\n"
"\n"
"1. Oda bilong Liklik Resolusen:\n"
"JPG PNG TIF BMP PDF  (yusim JPG pastaim, sapos i no gat orait PNG, TIF na ol narapela)\n"
"\n"
"2. Oda bilong Bikpela Resolusen:\n"
"TIF PNG JPG BMP PDF (yusim TIF pastaim, sapos i no gat orait PNG, JPG na ol narapela)\n"
"\n"
"O yu ken taipim wanpela oda bilong yu yet, olsem:\n"
"PDF TIF PNG (yusim PDF pastaim, sapos i no gat orait TIF, o PNG)\n"
"  o\n"
"JPG  (yusim JPG tasol - lusim ol narapela kain fail)\n"
"  o\n"
"TIF  (yusim TIF tasol - lusim ol narapela kain fail)\n"
"\n"
"TOKTOK: Ol TIF fail i kamap JPG hai-resolusen insait long program."

#: temp.glade:28586 temp.glade:28587
msgid "Include Pictures (illustrations)"
msgstr "Putim Piksa (ol piksa)"

#: temp.glade:28591
msgid "This setting enables/disables all the \n"
"other settings relating to pictures.\n"
"\n"
"Note that it is important to provide proper \n"
"copyright attribution for the illustrations \n"
"used in a publication, and this can be done\n"
"very easily using the \\zimagecopyrights\n"
"magic code within the Colophon (see\n"
"the Peripherals tab for details).\n"
msgstr "Dispela seting i op o pasim olgeta narapela seting bilong ol piksa.\n"
"\n"
"Save: i hatwok tumas long putim stretpela kopirait bilong ol piksa ol i yusim long wanpela publikesen, na yu ken mekim isi long yusim \\zimagecopyrights magic kod insait long Colophon (lukim Peripherals tab bilong kisim moa save).\n"

#: temp.glade:28652
msgid "Overview of the Pictures used in the publication."
msgstr "Lukluk long ol Piksa i stap long buk."

#: temp.glade:28653
msgid "Global Options"
msgstr "Ol Opsen bilong Olgeta"

#: temp.glade:28697 temp.glade:28725
msgid "The anchor specifies what page in a book a picture will appear on. It appears on the same page as its anchor in the text. You can alter the Anchor Ref by a few verses to change the page on which it appears.\n"
"\n"
"An Anchor Ref must consist of a book code, perhaps followed by L or R (in the case of a diglot), then a space, then an in-book location which contains a dot (period). In a scripture book, the in-book location is Chap.Verse where the Verse matches the \\v value precisely. In other books, the in-book location can be anything as long as it is unique in that book and contains a dot (period).\n"
"\n"
"Anchor Refs for Diglots use the L or R suffix on the 3-letter book code to indicate whether the picture is to be associated with the Primary (L) text or the Secondary (R) text.\n"
"\n"
"In the glossary book (GLO) there is special support for \\k Keywords\\k* where in-book location of k.keyword(s) will anchor a picture to the corresponding term. The in-book location must match the value of the \\k Keyword or phrase\\k* with its spaces removed. For example,\n"
"\n"
"    GLO k.Altar - would link it to \\k Altar\\k*\n"
"    GLO k.JohntheBaptist - would link a picture to\n"
"               a glossary entry \\k John the Baptist\\k*\n"
"\n"
"You can copy-and-paste a glossary word or phrase after typing GLO k. and PTXprint will automatically strip the spaces for you.\n"
"\n"
"Where there are no intervening anchors, you can anchor to the Nth paragraph of e.g. poetry or a keyterm definition, by specifying the paragraph number after an = sign. For example, GLO k.Harp=2 or PSA 23.4=3. This can avoid the need to insert an explicit milestone to anchor a cutout if there is a page or column break after the start of the verse."
msgstr "Anka i makim wanem pas long buk bai piksa i kamap long en. Piksa i kamap long sem pas wantaim anka bilong en long tekst. Yu ken senisim Anka Ref liklik ves long senisim pas we piksa i kamap long en.\n"
"\n"
"Anka Ref i mas gat kod bilong buk, na maski L o R i kam bihain (long diglot), na wanpela spes, na wanpela ples insait long buk i gat wanpela dot (poin). Long wanpela buk bilong Skripsa, ples insait long buk em Kapitel.Ves we Ves i mas sem stret wantaim \\v namba. Long ol narapela buk, ples insait long buk inap i stap wanem samting tasol sapos em i narapela long buk na i gat wanpela dot (poin).\n"
"\n"
"Anka Ref bilong ol Diglot i yusim L o R long las bilong 3-leta kod bilong buk long makim sapos piksa i bilong Pastaim tekst (L) o Namba Tu tekst (R).\n"
"\n"
"Long buk bilong glosari (GLO) i gat spesel sapot long \\k Keywords\\k* we ples insait long buk bilong k.keyword(s) i pasim wanpela piksa long dispela tok. Ples insait long buk i mas sem wantaim \\k Keyword o ol tok\\k* tasol ol spes i no stap. Olsem:\n"
"\n"
"    GLO k.Altar - i bai pasim wantaim \\k Altar\\k*\n"
"    GLO k.JohntheBaptist - i bai pasim wanpela piksa long\n"
"               wanpela glosari tok \\k John the Baptist\\k*\n"
"\n"
"Yu ken kopiim na pestim wanpela glosari tok o ol tok bihain long taipim GLO k. na PTXprint bai rausim ol spes yet.\n"
"\n"
"Sapos i no gat narapela anka namel, yu ken pasim long namba N paragraf bilong poetri o dispela bilong wanpela keyterm, long putim namba bilong paragraf bihain long wanpela = saen. Olsem, GLO k.Harp=2 o PSA 23.4=3. Dispela inap rausim nid bilong putim wanpela milestone long pasim wanpela cutout sapos i gat pas o kolum brek bihain long stat bilong ves."

#: temp.glade:28753
msgid "By default the caption will appear below the picture.\n"
"To show it above the picture, tick 'Show Caption\n"
"Before Image' on the Advanced tab (Other sub-tab,\n"
"Pictures, Figures, Images, Sidebars)."
msgstr "Olgeta taim, kaption i stap aninit long piksa. Bilong putim antap long piksa, putim mak long 'Show Caption Before Image' long Advanced tab (Other sub-tab, Pictures, Figures, Images, Sidebars)."

#: temp.glade:28769
msgid "By default, the caption will be followed by a Ch:Vs\n"
"reference in parentheses ( ). \n"
"\n"
"To put the Caption Ref BEFORE the caption text,\n"
"tick 'Ref Before Caption' on the Advanced tab\n"
"(Other sub-tab, Pictures, Figures, Images, Sidebars).\n"
"\n"
"To prevent Caption Refs from appearing globally,\n"
"use the Pictures > Global Options tab option:\n"
"    'Omit References (ch:vs)'"
msgstr "Olgeta taim, kaption i gat Ch:Vs refrens long bihain insait long kolam ( ).\n"
"\n"
"Bilong putim Caption Ref ANTAP long kaption tekst, putim mak long 'Ref Before Caption' long Advanced tab (Other sub-tab, Pictures, Figures, Images, Sidebars).\n"
"\n"
"Bilong pasim olgeta Caption Ref long kamap long olgeta ples, yusim opsen long Pictures > Global Options tab:\n"
"    'Omit References (ch:vs)'"

#: temp.glade:28782
msgid "Caption\n"
"Ref:"
msgstr "Kepsen\n"
"Ref:"

#: temp.glade:28798
msgid "The reference in the caption can be a single Ch:Vs or \n"
"a range of verses 6:17-29. This Caption Ref is different\n"
"from and independent of the Anchor Ref setting.\n"
msgstr "Ref long kepsen inap i stap wanpela Ch:Vs o\n"
"wanpela lain ves olsem 6:17-29. Dispela Kepsen Ref i narapela\n"
"na i no pasim Anka Ref seting.\n"

#: temp.glade:28816
msgid "Description:\n"
"(Alt Text)"
msgstr "Diskripsen:\n"
"(Alt Tekst)"

#: temp.glade:28844
msgid "Note that any changes you make to the filename\n"
"here will NOT automatically be updated in the\n"
"Paratext USFM files. Please edit/fit the figure\n"
"information manually in Paratext if you change\n"
"things here in PTXprint."
msgstr "Tingim olsem ol senis yu mekim long nem bilong fail\n"
"hia i NO bai senis yet long ol Paratext USFM fail. Plis\n"
"senisim ol infomesen bilong piksa long han insait long Paratext\n"
"sapos yu senisim ol samting hia long PTXprint."

#: temp.glade:28878
msgid "For commonly used series of illustrations, PTXprint\n"
"can automatically generate the appropriate copyright\n"
"attribution statement(s) as part of the colophon text.\n"
"\n"
"For other less-known artists' you may enter the appropriate\n"
"copyright information which is usually in the format of:\n"
"   by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type."
msgstr "Long ol kain piksa yumi save yusim planti taim, PTXprint\n"
"inap kamapim yet stetmen bilong kopirait\n"
"ol i stret olsem hap bilong kolofon tekst.\n"
"\n"
"Long ol narapela artist i no gat bikpela nem, yu ken putim\n"
"kopirait infomesen i stret, we i save kam olsem:\n"
"   by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type."

#: temp.glade:28886
msgid "Copyright\n"
"Attribution:"
msgstr "Kopirait\n"
"Atribiusen:"

#: temp.glade:28900
msgid "There are several shortcuts you can use:\n"
"   (c) --> ©  the copyright sign\n"
"   (r) --> ®  to denote registered trademarks\n"
"   (tm) --> ™  to denote trademarks in general"
msgstr "I gat sampela sotkat yu ken yusim:\n"
"   (c) --> ©  saen bilong kopirait\n"
"   (r) --> ®  long makim ol registered trademark\n"
"   (tm) --> ™  long makim ol trademark long olgeta"

#: temp.glade:28905
msgid "by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type"
msgstr "by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type"

#: temp.glade:28918
msgid "The frame size determines how large the picture\n"
"will appear on the page.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"When using single column layout, there is no\n"
"difference between Column Width and Span Width."
msgstr "Frem saiz i makim hamas bikpela piksa bai kamap long pas.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width i larim Antap o Daunbilo tasol.\n"
"Column Width i larim sampela narapela ples i stret moa: Bifor Ves, Bihain long Paragraf, o Cutout; na ol dispela\n"
"inap gat Left/Inner o Right/Outer Horizontal ples.\n"
" \n"
"Sapos yu yusim wanpela kolum tasol, i no gat\n"
"senis namel long Column Width na Span Width."

#: temp.glade:28941
msgid "Several options here are extensions to the normal USFM\n"
"markup standard for illustrations and are not expected\n"
"to work in other software. But PTXprint allows a greater\n"
"level of control in placing pictures.\n"
"\n"
"Top: Above everything except the header line\n"
"Bottom: Below all verse text (and footnotes in diglot)\n"
"Before Verse: 'Here' where defined or before its Anchor Ref\n"
"After Paragraph: After this paragraph\n"
"Cutout: A notch/corner cut out of the text, starting at current line\n"
"\n"
"The above options may have other positioning parameters such\n"
"as: Left, Right, Center, no. of lines (up or down)."
msgstr "Sampela opsen hia i ekstensen long stret USFM\n"
"makap bilong ol piksa na i no gat tingting olsem ol bai\n"
"wok long narapela software. Tasol PTXprint i larim moa\n"
"kontrol long putim ol piksa.\n"
"\n"
"Top: Antap long olgeta samting long hap hedalain\n"
"Bottom: Daunbilo long olgeta ves tekst (na futnot long diglot)\n"
"Before Ves: 'Hia' we i makim o bifor long Anka Ref bilong en\n"
"After Paragraf: Bihain long dispela paragraf\n"
"Cutout: Wanpela hap o kona i kat aut long tekst, i stat long lain nau\n"
"\n"
"Ol opsen antap inap gat narapela ples seting olsem:\n"
"Left, Right, Center, namba bilong ol lain (antap o daun)."

#: temp.glade:28969
msgid "An image (illustration) can be scaled to the\n"
"given size. This is particularly useful for\n"
"cutout images, and can prevent them from\n"
"taking up too much space within the text."
msgstr "Wanpela piksa inap kamap bikpela o liklik long\n"
"saiz yu givim. Dispela i gutpela tumas long\n"
"ol cutout piksa, na i ken stopim ol long\n"
"kisim planti ples insait long tekst."

#: temp.glade:28993
msgid "Several options here are extensions to the normal USFM\n"
"markup standard for illustrations and are not expected\n"
"to work in other software. But PTXprint allows a greater\n"
"level of control in placing pictures.\n"
"\n"
"Top: Above everything except the header line\n"
"Bottom: Below all verse text (and footnotes in diglot)\n"
"Below Notes: Below the footnotes (Span Width only)\n"
"Before Verse: 'Here' where defined or before its Anchor Ref\n"
"After Paragraph: After this paragraph\n"
"Cutout: A notch/corner cut out of the text, starting at current line\n"
"\n"
"The above options may have other positioning parameters such\n"
"as: Left, Right, Center, no. of lines (up or down)."
msgstr "Planti pasin long dispela lista i olsem extension long stendet USFM\n"
"markup bilong ol piksa, na i no gat save olsem ol narapela software bai wok long ol. Tasol PTXprint i larim yu kontrolim gutpela moa long ples bilong ol piksa.\n"
"\n"
"Top: Antap long olgeta samting tasol i no antap long header line\n"
"Bottom: Daunbilo long olgeta tok bilong ves (na ol footnote long diglot)\n"
"Below Notes: Daunbilo long ol footnote (Span Width tasol)\n"
"Before Verse: 'Hia' sapos i makim pinis o bipo long Anchor Ref bilong en\n"
"After Paragraph: Bihain long dispela paragraf\n"
"Cutout: Wanpela hul o kona i kisim ples long tok, i stat long lain bilong nau\n"
"\n"
"Ol pasin antap i ken gat narapela seting bilong ples olsem:\n"
"Left, Right, Center, namba bilong ol lain (i go antap o i go daun)."

#: temp.glade:29036
msgid "The frame size determines the boundaries of where the\n"
"picture will appear on the page.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n"
"\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"Page (in Margins) is intended for pictures that will cover an\n"
"entire page (i.e. preventing any scripture text from being on\n"
"that page), but will still show the header.\n"
"\n"
"Page (to Edge) is intended for pictures (or more commonly\n"
"for maps) to fill the entire page, with no margins at all. \n"
"Captions should not be used with 'Page (to Edge)' images."
msgstr "Frem saiz i makim ol bortpela bilong ples\n"
"piksa bai kamap long pas.\n"
"\n"
"Span Width i larim Antap o Daunbilo tasol.\n"
"\n"
"Column Width i larim sampela narapela ples i stret moa: Bifor Ves, Bihain long Paragraf, o Cutout; na ol dispela\n"
"inap gat Left/Inner o Right/Outer Horizontal ples.\n"
" \n"
"Page (in Margins) em bilong ol piksa i karamapim\n"
"olgeta pas (olsem i no gat Skripsa tekst long\n"
"dispela pas), tasol hedalain i stap yet.\n"
"\n"
"Page (to Edge) em bilong ol piksa (o moa long ol map)\n"
"long pulap olgeta pas, i no gat margin at all.\n"
"Ol kepsen i no ken yusim wantaim ol 'Page (to Edge)' piksa."

#: temp.glade:29129
msgid "It is good typesetting practice to make people\n"
"look outwards from the gutter, so you can set\n"
"whether the image is to be mirrored just on \n"
"odd pages or even pages.\n"
"\n"
"Some artists' pictures do not take into account\n"
"the \"dirty left-hand\" culture. For example, it would\n"
"be \"awkward\" to use a picture where Jesus is healing\n"
"a person using his LEFT hand! What an insult!\n"
"\n"
"So this option allows the image to be mirrored (on\n"
"both pages) in order to make the left become right.\n"
"But you should check carefully to see what other\n"
"unwanted side effects this mirroring may cause.\n"
"\n"
"Note: This option will be grayed out if the picture has  \n"
"the \"Never Mirror\" setting checked on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "Em i gutpela pasin bilong typesetting long mekim ol man\n"
"lukluk i go aut long gutter, olsem na yu ken makim\n"
"sapos piksa i mas mirror long odd pas tasol o even pas.\n"
"\n"
"Sampela piksa bilong ol artist i no tingim\n"
"kalsa bilong \"doti left-han\". Olsem, bai i\n"
"\"hevi\" long yusim piksa we Jisas i oraitim\n"
"wanpela man long LEFT han bilong em! Dispela i bikpela bagarap!\n"
"\n"
"Olsem na dispela opsen i larim piksa i mirror (long\n"
"olgeta tupela pas) long mekim left i kamap right.\n"
"Tasol yu mas lukim gut ol narapela hevi i no gutpela\n"
"mirror i ken kamapim.\n"
"\n"
"Toktok: Dispela opsen bai i kamap gre sapos piksa i gat\n"
"\"Never Mirror\" seting i makim long Checklist tab."

#: temp.glade:29147
msgid "Mirror:"
msgstr "Mirror:"

#: temp.glade:29162
msgid "Never = The image will never be mirrored\n"
"Odd = Mirrored only if image ends up on an odd page\n"
"Even = Mirrored only if image ends up on an even page\n"
"Always = Always mirrored (regardless of where it ends up)\n"
"\n"
"Note that if this option is grayed out, it is because \n"
"you have already restricted the mirroring options \n"
"on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "Never = Piksa i no inap mirror\n"
"Odd = Mirror sapos piksa i go long odd pas tasol\n"
"Even = Mirror sapos piksa i go long even pas tasol\n"
"Always = Mirror oltaim (maski em i go we)\n"
"\n"
"Tingim olsem sapos dispela opsen i gre, em i bikos\n"
"yu bin pasim pinis ol mirror opsen\n"
"long Checklist tab."

#: temp.glade:29197 temp.glade:29224
msgid "Some vertical position options allow a picture\n"
"to be moved up or down by a number of lines\n"
"or paragraphs.\n"
"\n"
"-Negative (minus) values specify to move UP.\n"
"+Positive (plus) values specify to move DOWN.\n"
"\n"
"Negative counts for cutouts raise the image,\n"
"but the cutout will not affect earlier paragraphs. \n"
"Note that negative and fractional paragraph \n"
"counts are invalid."
msgstr "Sampela vertikal ples opsen i larim wanpela piksa\n"
"long muv i go antap o daun long sampela lain\n"
"o paragraf.\n"
"\n"
"-Negatif (minus) namba i makim long muv i go ANTAP.\n"
"+Positif (plus) namba i makim long muv i go DAUN.\n"
"\n"
"Negatif namba bilong ol cutout i litimapim piksa,\n"
"tasol cutout i no ken senisim ol paragraf i go pastaim.\n"
"Tingim olsem negatif na hap namba bilong paragraf\n"
"i no stret."

#: temp.glade:29276
msgid "Can be used in Print/PDF publications. "
msgstr "Inap yusim long ol Print/PDF buk. "

#: temp.glade:29292
msgid "Can be used in mobile phone Apps. "
msgstr "Inap yusim long ol App bilong mobail fon. "

#: temp.glade:29308
msgid "Can be used on websites. "
msgstr "Inap yusim long ol websait. "

#: temp.glade:29329
msgid "If the image is from the recognized\n"
"set of pictures commonly used in\n"
"Scripture publications, then there is\n"
"no need to fill in the Copyright \n"
"Attribution field, as this will be\n"
"generated automatically for you."
msgstr "Sapos dispela piksa i stap insait long ol piksa\n"
"ol i save yusim long ol buk bilong Skripsa,\n"
"na i no gat nid long pulim Copyright\n"
"Attribution field, long wanem dispela bai\n"
"i kamap yet long em yet."

#: temp.glade:29337
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr "Otomatik"

#: temp.glade:29349
msgid "© ..."
msgstr ""

#: temp.glade:29354
msgid "Credit Overlays...\n"
"Some artists (e.g. David C Cook) require that\n"
"each image has a copyright message printed\n"
"on the image itself. The text and location can\n"
"be set here."
msgstr "Credit Overlays...\n"
"Sampela artist (olsem David C Cook) i laik olgeta piksa\n"
"i gat wanpela toktok bilong copyright i stap\n"
"long piksa yet. Ken makim tekst na ples bilong en\n"
"long hia."

#: temp.glade:29376
msgid "Credit overlay position and style"
msgstr "Ples na stail bilong credit overlay"

#: temp.glade:29422
msgid "Click to edit the Figure Caption properties on the Styles tab."
msgstr "Klikim long senisim ol propeti bilong Figure Caption long Styles tab."

#: temp.glade:29447 temp.glade:29472
msgid "One or more optional (x-xetex) attributes \n"
"can be applied for rotation and/or PDF page\n"
"selection. For example:\n"
"rotated 90     - anti-clockwise\n"
"rotate=edge     - top to outside edge\n"
"rotate=binding    - top to binding edge\n"
"page=2     - select page 2 of multi-page PDF\n"
"\n"
"Multiple parameters should be space-separated:\n"
"rotate=binding page=2"
msgstr "Yu ken putim wanpela o moa (x-xetex) attribute (i no mas)\n"
"long tanim piksa na/o makim peisim bilong PDF. Olsem:\n"
"rotated 90     - i tanim i go long han kais\n"
"rotate=edge     - antap i go long arere bilong ausait\n"
"rotate=binding    - antap i go long arere bilong binding\n"
"page=2     - makim peis 2 bilong PDF i gat planti peis\n"
"\n"
"Sapos yu putim planti seting, yu mas rausim ol long wanpela spes:\n"
"rotate=binding page=2"

#: temp.glade:29458
msgid "Extra:"
msgstr "Extra:"

#: temp.glade:29567
msgid "Use this tab to change the position, location, size \n"
"or orientation of the images.\n"
"\n"
"Note: Any changes you make here will NOT be \n"
"reflected in the Paratext USFM files. So if you are \n"
"changing an illustration, its caption or frame size\n"
"(column or span), then it is advisable to do so\n"
"in Paratext before regenerating the PicList here."
msgstr "Yusim dispela tab long senisim ples, saiz o pasin bilong\n"
"ol piksa i sanap.\n"
"\n"
"Not: Ol senis yu mekim long hia i NO inap kamap\n"
"long ol Paratext USFM fail. Olsem na sapos yu laik\n"
"senisim wanpela piksa, caption bilong en o saiz bilong frame\n"
"(column o span), orait gutpela yu mekim long\n"
"Paratext pastaim bipo yu kamapim gen PicList long hia."

#: temp.glade:29575
msgid "Details"
msgstr "Detels"

#: temp.glade:29632
msgid "Is there anything confusing or misleading in this image that the reader might misunderstand if they look at this picture apart from the text? Yes and no are both appropriate answers as some images may need to be seen alongside text in order to be understood."
msgstr "Ating gat wanpela samting long dispela piksa i mekim ol man i les o i no stret, na ol rider i ken kisim tingting i no stret sapos ol i lukim piksa tasol, i no gat tekst? Yes na No tupela i ken stret, long wanem sampela piksa i mas lukim wantaim tekst bambai ol i ken save."

#: temp.glade:29634
msgid "Is it clear what is happening in this image?"
msgstr "I klia long wanem samting i go het long dispela piksa?"

#: temp.glade:29645
msgid "First consider whether this picture is appropriate and culturally acceptable in any publications for this project."
msgstr "Pastaim tingim sapos dispela piksa i stret na kalsa i orait long olgeta pablikesen bilong dispela projek."

#: temp.glade:29647
msgid "Across Various Publications:"
msgstr "Long Ol Narapela Pablikesen:"

#: temp.glade:29661 temp.glade:29929 temp.glade:29983
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "Yes"

#: temp.glade:29679 temp.glade:29947 temp.glade:30001
msgid "No"
msgstr "No"

#: temp.glade:29717
msgid "Be sure that there is nothing offensive or inappropriate in this image. This could be the way people are clothed, what actions they are doing, how they are depicted, etc. “Culturally Appropriate” means this image is in a style from this culture or a related one, “Acceptable” means this picture might be from a different culture or in a different style, but there are no issues using it. “Inappropriate” means there are issues that should prevent this image from being used. Answering “Inappropriate” will help avoid this image being used in other publications."
msgstr "Lukim gut olsem i no gat wanpela samting long dispela piksa i mekim ol man i belhat o i no stret. Em inap long pasin bilong ol i werim klos, wanem pasin ol i mekim, o olsem wanem ol i soim ol, na ol narapela. “Culturally Appropriate” i min piksa i gat stail bilong dispela kalsa o narapela i klostu long en. “Acceptable” i min piksa inap kam long narapela kalsa o gat narapela stail, tasol i no gat hevi long yusim. “Inappropriate” i min i gat hevi i mekim olsem ol i no ken yusim dispela piksa. Sapos yu bekim “Inappropriate”, bai i helpim long no ken yusim dispela piksa long ol narapela pablikesen."

#: temp.glade:29719
msgid "Is this image acceptable in your culture?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa i orait long kalsa bilong yu?"

#: temp.glade:29730
msgid "Sometimes mirroring (reversing) an image makes it\n"
"acceptable since a left hand becomes a right hand, etc.\n"
"\n"
"Some artists' pictures do not take into account\n"
"the \"dirty left-hand\" culture. For example, it would\n"
"be \"awkward\" to use a picture where Jesus is healing\n"
"a person using his left hand!"
msgstr "Sampela taim sapos yumi tanim (tainim) piksa, em i kamap orait,\n"
"bikos han kais i kamap han sut, na olsem.\n"
"\n"
"Sampela piksa bilong ol artist i no tingim\n"
"pasin bilong \"han kais i doti\". Olsem, bai i no gutpela\n"
"sapos yumi yusim piksa we Jisas i helim wanpela man\n"
"wantaim han kais bilong em!"

#: temp.glade:29738
msgid "Would the image be culturally acceptable if \n"
"the image was mirrored (left becomes right)?"
msgstr "Sapos yumi tanim piksa (han kais i kamap han sut),\n"
"em i orait long kalsa o nogat?"

#: temp.glade:29750 temp.glade:30072
msgid "Now consider whether there are any issues with using this picture in this particular publication (config-specific)."
msgstr "Nau tingim sapos i gat wanpela hevi long yusim dispela piksa long dispela pablikesen (config-specific)."

#: temp.glade:29752
msgid "In This Publication:"
msgstr "Long Dispela Pablikesen:"

#: temp.glade:29768
msgid "Consider how this image is used alongside the text and what function it serves. Maybe it depicts a building or item from a biblical culture, or a scene from a story."
msgstr "Tingim olsem wanem dispela piksa i stap wantaim tekst na wanem wok em i mekim. Ating em i soim wanpela haus o samting bilong kalsa bilong Baibel, o wanpela senis bilong stori."

#: temp.glade:29770
msgid "Is this picture intended for: clarification,\n"
"story enhancement, filler, unknown?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa em bilong wanem: skelim klia,\n"
"mekim stori i strong, pulapim ples, o i no save?"

#: temp.glade:29782
msgid "Does the image support what the text is saying? As they read the passage does the image help in their understanding?"
msgstr "Piksa i sapotim tok bilong tekst o nogat? Taim ol i ritim dispela hap, piksa i helpim ol long save?"

#: temp.glade:29784
msgid "In the context of this passage, is it clear \n"
"what is happening in this image?"
msgstr "Long dispela hap tok, ating klia long wanem samting i kamap long dispela piksa?"

#: temp.glade:29796
msgid "For example, do the colors have the same meaning in the local culture? Is there anything in the background that is distracting from the story? Are there any objects, gestures, or other things that imply something unintended or that isn’t in the passage? Are there any anachronisms in the picture (a minaret in Bethlehem)?"
msgstr "Olsem, ol kala i gat wankain minin long ples bilong yupela? I gat wanpela samting long baksait i save paulim tingting long stori? I gat wanpela samting, pasin bilong han o narapela samting i makim wanpela tok i no stap long dispela hap tok? I gat wanpela samting long piksa i no stret long taim (olsem wanpela minaret long Betlehem)?"

#: temp.glade:29798
msgid "Does the image communicate something \n"
"that it should not in this particular context?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa i soim wanpela samting\n"
"em i no ken soim long dispela taim?"

#: temp.glade:29810
msgid "Do the images and their style fit with the type of publication, i.e. Scripture, children’s materials, lectionary, etc.? Are people and actions depicted in acceptable ways?"
msgstr "Ol piksa na stail bilong ol i stret long kain buk yupela i wokim, olsem Skripsa, ol buk bilong ol pikinini, lektionari, na ol narapela? Ol man na ol pasin i soim long piksa, i orait long ol man?"

#: temp.glade:29812
msgid "Is the image appropriate for the publication?"
msgstr "Dispela piksa i stret long dispela buk?"

#: temp.glade:29825
msgid "Select the level to which this illustration\n"
"is acceptable in the receptor culture."
msgstr "Makim hamas dispela piksa\n"
"i orait long kalsa bilong ol man i kisim."

#: temp.glade:29842
msgid "OK to\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "I OK long\n"
"mirror"

#: temp.glade:29848
msgid "It is fine to mirror the image if needed. It would\n"
"not change the impact or response of the readers."
msgstr "I orait long mirrorim dispela piksa sapos i gat bikpela as. Dispela i no senisim tingting o bekim bilong ol man i ritim."

#: temp.glade:29863
msgid "Never\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "Nogat\n"
"mirror"

#: temp.glade:29869
msgid "Ensure that this image is always shown\n"
"as currently depicted in the preview. Do\n"
"NOT allow it to be mirrored (reversed)."
msgstr "Mekim sure dispela piksa i stap oltaim\n"
"olsem em i stap long preview nau. Nogat\n"
"mirrorim (tainim) em."

#: temp.glade:29885
msgid "Always\n"
"mirror"
msgstr "Oltaim\n"
"mirror"

#: temp.glade:29891
msgid "Ensure that this image is always mirrored from\n"
"what is currently shown in the preview. Therefore\n"
"actions being done with the left hand will show as\n"
"being done with the right hand, and vice versa."
msgstr "Mekim sure dispela piksa i stap mirror oltaim\n"
"bilong dispela i stap long preview nau. Olsem na\n"
"wok ol i mekim long han kais bai i kamap olsem\n"
"ol i mekim long han skru, na sem tasol."

#: temp.glade:29912
msgid "Select the reason for including the\n"
"illustration in this particular publication."
msgstr "Makim as bilong putim dispela\n"
"piksa long dispela buk."

#: temp.glade:29965 temp.glade:30051
msgid "Unchecked"
msgstr "I no gat setik"

#: temp.glade:30023
msgid "Select the appropriateness of the\n"
"illustration within this publication."
msgstr "Makim olsem wanem dispela piksa\n"
"i stret long dispela buk."

#: temp.glade:30074
msgid "Consultant Approval:"
msgstr "Konsultan i orait:"

#: temp.glade:30091
msgid "The most recent date that the\n"
"consultant approval updated."
msgstr "Las dei long konsultan i senisim\n"
"orait bilong em."

#: temp.glade:30097
msgid "Date"
msgstr "Dei"

#: temp.glade:30114
msgid "Initials"
msgstr "Nem bilong yu (initial)"

#: temp.glade:30128
msgid "any publication"
msgstr "olgeta buk"

#: temp.glade:30145
msgid "this publication"
msgstr "dispela buk"

#: temp.glade:30162
msgid "Approved to\n"
"be used in:"
msgstr "I orait long\n"
"yusim long:"

#: temp.glade:30181
msgid "     "
msgstr ""

#: temp.glade:30194
msgid "By:"
msgstr "Long:"

#: temp.glade:30258
msgid "Use the notes area below to record anything \n"
"about this picture, or to dialog with the consultant.\n"
"The notes entered here are saved with this\n"
"configuration only (other configurations have their own)."
msgstr "Yusim ples bilong ol nots daunbilo long raitim wanem samting\n"
"about long dispela piksa, o long toktok wantaim konsaltent.\n"
"Ol nots yu raitim hia i stap long dispela configuration tasol\n"
"(ol narapela configuration i gat ol nots bilong ol yet)."

#: temp.glade:30263
msgid "Notes About This Picture:"
msgstr "Ol not long dispela piksa:"

#: temp.glade:30343
msgid "Pictures are best used in situations where:\n"
"1. The physical situation is not understood, or not common in the target culture.\n"
"2. Where the physical situation is important to understanding the meaning of the passage (e.g., the type of clothing is often not important, but in some passages it might be).\n"
"3. Where they help the reader to understand the passage.\n"
"4. Where it entices the reader to read the passage."
msgstr "Ol piksa i gutpela long ol taim olsem:\n"
"1. Ol man i no save long dispela samting, o i no planti long kalsa bilong ol.\n"
"2. Samting long ai i bikpela long save long minin bilong dispela hap tok (olsem, kain laplap i no save bikpela, tasol long sampela hap tok em i ken bikpela).\n"
"3. Ol i helpim man i ritim long kliaim dispela hap tok.\n"
"4. Ol i pulim tingting bilong man long ritim dispela hap tok."

#: temp.glade:30348
msgid "Questions to Consider"
msgstr "Ol Askim long Skelim"

#: temp.glade:30377
msgid "This tab encourages you to think through\n"
"the appropriateness of the pictures used\n"
"in this publication, as well as other contexts."
msgstr "Dispela tab i helpim yu long tingting gut\n"
"long ol piksa yu yusim long dispela buk,\n"
"na long ol narapela ples tu."

#: temp.glade:30380
msgid "Checklist"
msgstr "Lis bilong Skelim"

#: temp.glade:30475
msgid "Manipulate the pictures to be used\n"
"in the publication. Control everything\n"
"from quality to position, from captions\n"
"to copyrights."
msgstr "Stretim ol piksa bilong ol i go insait\n"
"long buk. Yu ken kontrolim olgeta samting\n"
"stat long kwaliti na ples, na tu ol caption\n"
"na ol kopirait."

#: temp.glade:30524
msgid "Use Default Header Settings for Diglot"
msgstr "Yusim Seting Bilong Header i Stap Pastaim Long Diglot"

#: temp.glade:30529
msgid "Checking this option will override\n"
"the header settings and place the\n"
"Reference Ranges on the outer edges\n"
"and Page Number in (or near) the middle."
msgstr "Sapos yu makim dispela, ol seting bilong header\n"
"i no moa wok, na ol Reference Ranges bai i go\n"
"long ol sait ausait na namba bilong pes bai i stap\n"
"long namel (o klostu long namel)."

#: temp.glade:30545
msgid "Adjust Center Header Based on Column Widths"
msgstr "Senisim Header Namel Folim Bikpela Bilong Ol Kolum"

#: temp.glade:30550
msgid "If the column widths of the two sides of the\n"
"diglot are unequal, PTXprint can ensure that\n"
"the content of the center header matches the\n"
"position of the gutter (space between the two\n"
"different columns)."
msgstr "Sapos ol kolum long tupela sait bilong diglot\n"
"i no wankain bikpela, PTXprint i ken mekim\n"
"olsem ol samting long header namel i stap\n"
"stret long gutter (spes namel long tupela\n"
"kolum)."

#: temp.glade:30588
msgid "Vertical Rule in Notes Area"
msgstr "Vertikal Rule Long Ples Bilong Ol Nout"

#: temp.glade:30593
msgid "Add a vertical rule between the two\n"
"sides of the notes area of the diglot."
msgstr "Putim wanpela vertikal rule namel long tupela\n"
"sait bilong ples bilong ol nout bilong diglot."

#: temp.glade:30608
msgid "Join with Rule Above"
msgstr "Joinim Wantaim Rule i Stap Antap"

#: temp.glade:30613
msgid "To prevent a small gap in the line\n"
"allow the vertical line to extend\n"
"down into the notes area."
msgstr "Bilong stopim liklik spes long lain,\n"
"larim vertikal lain i go daun\n"
"long ples bilong ol nout."

#: temp.glade:30632
msgid "Separate Notes in Two Columns"
msgstr "Katim Ol Nout Long Tupela Kolum"

#: temp.glade:30637
msgid "If this option is disabled, the footnotes from\n"
"both sides of the diglot get merged together\n"
"and are interspersed one after the other.\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the scripts and text direction,\n"
"this may or may not be desirable. If in doubt,\n"
"leave this option checked ON."
msgstr "Sapos dispela i no makim, ol futnout\n"
"bilong tupela sait bilong diglot i kamap wantaim\n"
"na i stap wan bihain long narapela.\n"
"\n"
"Tingting long ol skripsa na direksen bilong tok,\n"
"sampela taim dispela i gutpela o i no gutpela.\n"
"Sapos yu no save, larim dispela i stap makim (ON)."

#: temp.glade:30692
msgid "Left-click to change values as needed.\n"
"Right-click to show the context menu."
msgstr "Klikim long lephan sait bilong senisim ol velyu.\n"
"Klikim long raitan sait bilong lukim context menu."

#: temp.glade:30740 temp.glade:30897
msgid "The Layout string describes how\n"
"the various texts should appear\n"
"on the page(s).\n"
"\n"
"All of the texts listed in the table\n"
"above must be mentioned. The\n"
"comma represents the next page.\n"
"A forward slash / will put one\n"
"text under the other on the same\n"
"page (this is still to come and\n"
"cannot be used yet)."
msgstr "Layout string i stori long wanem pasin\n"
"ol different tok i mas kamap\n"
"long ol peis.\n"
"\n"
"Olgeta tok i stap long tebel antap\n"
"i mas stap insait. Koma i makim\n"
"nekis peis. Wanpela slash / bai\n"
"putim wanpela tok aninit long narapela\n"
"long sem peis (dispela i no redi yet\n"
"na yu no inap yusim nau)."

#: temp.glade:30756
msgid "LR,A/B"
msgstr "LR,A/B"

#: temp.glade:30775 temp.glade:30806 temp.glade:30830
msgid "When the different texts of a diglot are merged, there are various \n"
"algorithms which may be used to obtain the best overall result:\n"
"\n"
"* Chapter Verse - aligns on chapters and verses\n"
"\n"
"* Scored - an alternative algorithm which uses weighted scores\n"
"  and tries to align paragraphs when the verse numbers match\n"
"\n"
"* Scored (Chapter) - as a minimum, forces alignment at chapter breaks\n"
"\n"
"* Scored (Verse) - as a minimum, forces alignment at each verse, which \n"
"  can result in a lot of breaks!\n"
"\n"
"Note that for polyglots, only the Scored options are available to be used."
msgstr "Taim ol different tok bilong diglot i kamap wanpela, i gat ol different\n"
"algorithm yu ken yusim long kisim gutpela as result:\n"
"\n"
"* Chapter Verse - i makim wantaim long ol kapitel na ol ves\n"
"\n"
"* Scored - narapela algorithm i yusim ol skor i gat wet\n"
"  na i traim long makim ol paragraf taim namba bilong ves i wankain\n"
"\n"
"* Scored (Chapter) - liklik tru, i fosim makim wantaim long ol brek bilong kapitel\n"
"\n"
"* Scored (Verse) - liklik tru, i fosim makim wantaim long olgeta ves, \n"
"  na dispela i ken mekim planti brek!\n"
"\n"
"Notim olsem long polyglot, ol Scored options tasol i ken yusim."

#: temp.glade:30791
msgid "Merging mode:"
msgstr "Rot bilong joinim:"

#: temp.glade:30873
msgid "Auto calculate primary percentage by trying to reduce the page count. This will run your print job up to 10 times or more, so choose a small book to run on. It will attempt to find the best balance of column widths near to the current % Width values. Only available for a diglot with two texts."
msgstr "Kalkulesim primary percentage yet long traim daunim namba bilong ol peis. Dispela bai ranim print job bilong yu inap 10 taim o moa, olsem na makim wanpela liklik buk. Em bai traim long painim gutpela balans bilong wait bilong ol kolum klostu long ol % Width value bilong nau. I stap long diglot i gat tupela tok tasol."

#: temp.glade:30911
msgid "Layout:"
msgstr "Layout:"

#: temp.glade:30923 temp.glade:30946
msgid "Some books (e.g. Introduction, Glossary, Back Matter, etc.)\n"
"in a diglot publication should not be merged to appear\n"
"side-by-side, but instead need to occur one after the other.\n"
"\n"
"Add the 3-letter book codes for any books that should \n"
"not be merged. These will appear one after the other."
msgstr "Sampela buk (olsem Introduction, Glossary, Back Matter, na ol narapela)\n"
"long wanpela diglot i no ken joinim long kamap sait long sait,\n"
"nogat, ol i mas kamap wan bihain long narapela.\n"
"\n"
"Putim ol kod bilong ol buk (3 leta) we yu no laik joinim.\n"
"Ol bai kamap wan bihain long narapela."

#: temp.glade:30931
msgid "Use Serial Layout\n"
"for These Books:"
msgstr "Yusim Serial Layout\n"
"Long Ol Dispela Buk:"

#: temp.glade:30955
msgid "FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"
msgstr "FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"

#: temp.glade:30957
msgid "e.g. FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"
msgstr "olsem FRT BAK GLO XXA XXB"

#: temp.glade:30968
msgid "Diglot (or Polyglot)"
msgstr "Diglot (o Polyglot)"

#: temp.glade:30973
msgid "A Diglot publication contains two\n"
"languages, or scripts, or texts.\n"
"\n"
"A Polyglot contains more than two.\n"
"Right-click in the table below to\n"
"add other texts to the list.\n"
"\n"
"Tip: use Save As first. Unticking this\n"
"later does not simply switch back; it\n"
"offers to save a single-text copy of\n"
"the configuration under a new name."
msgstr "Diglot publikesen i gat tupela\n"
"languis, o skript, o tok.\n"
"\n"
"Polyglot i gat moa long tupela.\n"
"Rait-klikim long tebel daunbilo long\n"
"kirapim ol narapela tok i go long lista.\n"
"\n"
"Tip: Yusim Save As pastaim. Sapos yu rausim tik bihain,\n"
"em i no tanim i go bek tasol; em i askim yu long seivim\n"
"kopi bilong wanpela tok tasol long nupela nem."

#: temp.glade:31006
msgid "Create a diglot publication by selecting \n"
"a secondary project and configuration."
msgstr "Kamapim wanpela diglot buk long makim\n"
"wanpela narapela projek na configuration."

#: lib/ptxprint/gtkstyleditor.py:65 lib/ptxprint/gtkview.py:3049
msgid "Diglot"
msgstr "Diglot"

#: temp.glade:31051 temp.glade:31188
msgid "The length of the Thumb Tab measured in millimeters (mm)."
msgstr "Longpela bilong Thumb Tab, ol i makim long milimita (mm)."

#: temp.glade:31053
msgid "Length:"
msgstr "Longpela:"

#: temp.glade:31065 temp.glade:31080
msgid "The height of the Thumb Tab measured in millimeters (mm)."
msgstr "Hait bilong Thumb Tab, ol i makim long milimita (mm)."

#: temp.glade:31067
msgid "Height:"
msgstr "Hait:"

#: temp.glade:31100
msgid "Thumb Tabs usually use a dark color\n"
"for the background with a light color\n"
"(or white) for the foreground text.\n"
"\n"
"The background color is set here, but\n"
"the foreground text color needs to be\n"
"set by clicking the Edit Style link."
msgstr "Thumb Tab i save usim kala i strong\n"
"long baksait, na kala i lait (o wait)\n"
"long tok i stap antap.\n"
"\n"
"Yu makim kala bilong baksait hia, tasol\n"
"yu mas makim kala bilong tok long klikim\n"
"link Edit Style."

#: temp.glade:31108
msgid "Tab Color:"
msgstr "Kala bilong Tab:"

#: temp.glade:31122
msgid "The background color of the tabs. Use a dark color\n"
"here and set the light text color with the Edit Style link."
msgstr "Kala bilong baksait bilong ol tab. Yusim wanpela tudak kala\n"
"hia na makim lait kala bilong tok long Edit Style link."

#: temp.glade:31125
msgid "Thumb Tab Background Color"
msgstr "Kala bilong baksait bilong Thumb Tab"

#: temp.glade:31136
msgid "Rotate Tabs:"
msgstr "Tanim ol Tab:"

#: temp.glade:31141
msgid "Rotates the tabs so that the text runs along the edge of the page. This works well for narrow margins, but may result in fewer tab positions per page."
msgstr "Tanim ol tab olsem tok i go sait long hap bilong pes. Dispela i gutpela long margin i liklik, tasol ol tab i ken kamap lukim wanpela pes i stap liklik."

#: temp.glade:31157
msgid "How many tabs can there be down a page. This is automatically calculated from the Height (or Length when rotated), Page size and Margins. If any of these change then this value will be updated. Increasing it, makes tabs overlap. Reducing it spreads them apart."
msgstr "Hamas tab i ken stap long wanpela peis. Dispela i kalkulesim yet long Height (o Length taim i tanim), Page size na ol Margin. Sapos wanpela bilong ol dispela i senis, dispela namba bai senis tu. Sapos yu mekim i bikpela, ol tab i go antap long ol narapela. Sapos yu mekim i liklik, ol tab i go longwe long ol narapela."

#: temp.glade:31159
msgid "Number of\n"
"Tab Positions:"
msgstr "Hamas\n"
"ples bilong Tab:"

#: temp.glade:31212 temp.glade:31314
msgid "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  Vertical  </span>"
msgstr "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  Vertical  </span>"

#: temp.glade:31229 temp.glade:31345
msgid "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  Horizontal  </span>"
msgstr "<span background=\"black\" foreground=\"white\" font-weight=\"bold\">  Horizontal  </span>"

#: temp.glade:31243
msgid "When several shorter adjacent books occur, it is\n"
"common to group them together to use the same\n"
"tab position (but still have differently named tabs)."
msgstr "Sapos sampela liklik buk i stap klostu\n"
"long ol narapela, ol i save putim ol wantaim\n"
"long usim wankain ples bilong tab (tasol ol tab i gat narapela narapela nem)."

#: temp.glade:31248
msgid "Grouped Tabs:"
msgstr "Ol Tab i Go Wantaim:"

#: temp.glade:31261
msgid "List book IDs of short books to be grouped together\n"
"at the same tab position. Use spaces between book \n"
"IDs, and use ; to separate groups. There is no need to\n"
"list all the book IDs here - only the special ones which\n"
"need to share the same tab position.\n"
"\n"
"For example: PHM TIT; 1JN 2JN 3JN JUD"
msgstr "Putim ol ID bilong ol liklik buk we yu laik putim wantaim\n"
"long wankain ples bilong tab. Putim spes namel long ol\n"
"ID bilong buk, na usim ; long skelim ol grup. Yu no\n"
"mas putim olgeta ID bilong buk hia - ol buk tasol we\n"
"i mas bihainim wankain ples bilong tab.\n"
"\n"
"Pastaim: PHM TIT; 1JN 2JN 3JN JUD"

#: temp.glade:31283
msgid "If you choose to Rotate the tabs, there are various options as to how these should be oriented. The preview (right) will show how these will appear on facing pages."
msgstr "Sapos yu makim long Tanim ol tab, i gat sampela rot bilong makim olsem wanem ol i mas sanap. Preview (long rait) bai soim olsem wanem ol i kamap long ol pes i stap wantaim."

#: temp.glade:31371
msgid "Restart Tabs at MAT"
msgstr "Statim gen ol Tab long MAT"

#: temp.glade:31376
msgid "Normally books will follow sequentially and if the next tab would be off the bottom of the page, then it will be set to the top for a new cycle of tabs. Setting this starts a new cycle at the start of the New Testament (Matthew)."
msgstr "Long stret pasin ol buk i bihainim wanpela wanpela, na sapos tab i kamap i go daun long pes, em bai i go long antap long statim nupela lain bilong ol tab. Sapos yu makim dispela, nupela lain i statim long stat bilong Nupela Testamen (Matyu)."

#: temp.glade:31393
msgid "ColorVal"
msgstr "ColorVal"

#: temp.glade:31407
msgid "Clicking this button will replace the\n"
"Grouped Tabs list with the default groups."
msgstr "Sapos yu klikim dispela boton, em bai senisim\n"
"lista bilong Grouped Tabs long ol default group."

#: temp.glade:31474
msgid "Tab Text:"
msgstr "Tok bilong Tab:"

#: temp.glade:31484
msgid "\\toc3"
msgstr "Toktok"

#: temp.glade:31489
msgid "By default, Thumb Tabs use the content and styling of the \\toc3 marker.\n"
"\n"
"Note that this setting is interconnected with the Table of Contents settings \n"
"on the Peripherals tab. If \\toc3 is not included in the ToC, then this option\n"
"will be disabled. So it is recommended to use \\toc3 as your thumbtab text \n"
"and include it in the Table of Contents. "
msgstr "Olgeta taim, ol Thumb Tab i yusim kontent na styling bilong \\toc3 marker.\n"
"\n"
"Notim olsem dispela seting i pas wantaim ol seting bilong Table of Contents\n"
"long Peripherals tab. Sapos \\toc3 i no stap insait long ToC, orait dispela option\n"
"bai i no wok. Olsem na gutpela yu yusim \\toc3 olsem tok bilong thumbtab\n"
"na putim insait long Table of Contents. "

#: temp.glade:31510
msgid "\\zthumbtab"
msgstr "Toktok wantaim ol narapela"

#: temp.glade:31515
msgid "By default, Thumb Tabs use the content and styling of the \\toc3 marker.\n"
"If you prefer different content and/or styling for the tabs, then this\n"
"\\zthumbtab option needs to be enabled, and the thumbtab names\n"
"entered into your USFM text.\n"
"\n"
"Note that this setting is interconnected with the Table of Contents settings \n"
"on the Peripherals tab. If \\toc3 is not included in the ToC, then you are \n"
"forced to use the \\zthumbtab setting here. For that reason it is highly \n"
"recommended to use \\toc3 as your thumbtab text and include it in \n"
"the Table of Contents. \n"
"\n"
"The USFM extension \\zthumbtab can be used to set an alternative value for \n"
"the thumbtab contents. If a book's header contains a \\zthumbtab entry, then \n"
"\\toc3 will not be used as the thumbtab contents. An empty \\zthumbtab entry \n"
"specifies that there should be no text in the thumbtab for that book."
msgstr "Olgeta taim, ol Thumb Tab i yusim kontent na styling bilong \\toc3 marker.\n"
"Sapos yu laikim narapela kontent na/o styling bilong ol tab, orait\n"
"dispela \\zthumbtab option i mas wok, na ol nem bilong thumbtab\n"
"i mas stap insait long USFM tok bilong yu.\n"
"\n"
"Notim olsem dispela seting i pas wantaim ol seting bilong Table of Contents\n"
"long Peripherals tab. Sapos \\toc3 i no stap insait long ToC, orait yu mas\n"
"yusim \\zthumbtab seting hia. Long dispela as, i gutpela tumas\n"
"yu yusim \\toc3 olsem tok bilong thumbtab na putim insait long\n"
"Table of Contents.\n"
"\n"
"USFM extension \\zthumbtab i ken yusim long putim narapela tok bilong\n"
"kontent bilong thumbtab. Sapos header bilong wanpela buk i gat \\zthumbtab, orait\n"
"bai ol i no yusim \\toc3 olsem kontent bilong thumbtab. \\zthumbtab i no gat samting insait\n"
"i makim olsem i no gat tok long thumbtab bilong dispela buk."

#: lib/ptxprint/pdf_viewer.py:59
msgid "Edit Style"
msgstr "Senisim Style"

#: temp.glade:31550
msgid "Click to jump to the appropriate\n"
"(\\toc3 or \\zthumbtab) marker in\n"
"the style editor to change the\n"
"formatting of the thumb tabs."
msgstr "Klikim long go long marker (\\toc3 o \\zthumbtab) i stret\n"
"long style editor long senisim\n"
"stail bilong ol thumb tab."

#: temp.glade:31574
msgid "Only Show on Odd Pages"
msgstr "Soim long Odd Pes tasol"

#: temp.glade:31579
msgid "When printing thumb tabs on thin paper,\n"
"it is preferable to only print these tabs on\n"
"a single side of the page (the odd pages)."
msgstr "Taim yu printim ol thumb tab long pepa i spak,\n"
"em i gutpela long printim ol tab long\n"
"wanpela sait tasol bilong pes (ol odd pes)."

#: temp.glade:31597
msgid "Thumb Tabs"
msgstr "Thumb Tab"

#: temp.glade:31602
msgid "Thumb Tabs are sometimes used in longer publications to help the user find a scripture book more easily. By default\n"
"these use the \\toc3 element in a USFM file to provide\n"
"the text for the tab.\n"
"Note: If only a single book is currently selected, it will place the Thumb Tab relative to ALL the books listed in the multiple book list."
msgstr "Ol Thumb Tab ol i save yusim long ol longpela publikesen long helpim ol man painim wanpela buk bilong Skripsa isi moa. Olgeta taim\n"
"ol i yusim \\toc3 element long wanpela USFM fail long kisim\n"
"tok bilong tab.\n"
"Notim: Sapos wanpela buk tasol i makim nau, em bai putim Thumb Tab long ples i go wantaim OLGETA buk i stap long lista bilong planti buk."

#: temp.glade:31700 temp.glade:31717
msgid "Vertical shift in pts of the section box image.\n"
"  + values shift the box upwards\n"
"  - values shift the box downwards"
msgstr "Sip long antap o daunbilo bilong piksa bilong section box long pts.\n"
"  + namba i sipim box i go antap\n"
"  - namba i sipim box i go daun"

#: temp.glade:31704 temp.glade:32359
msgid "Shift:"
msgstr "Sip:"

#: temp.glade:31735
msgid "Scale section header image. 1.0 = its own size,\n"
"0.5 = half size, 2.0 = double size."
msgstr "Senisim bikpela bilong piksa bilong section header. 1.0 = sem bikpela bilong en yet,\n"
"0.5 = hap bikpela, 2.0 = tupela bikpela."

#: temp.glade:31765 temp.glade:31975
msgid "PDF border (Legacy)"
msgstr "PDF border (Legacy)"

#: temp.glade:31769
msgid "Place a PDF graphic behind each section\n"
"heading (\\s, \\s1, \\s2). Use Select... to\n"
"choose it, and Scale/Shift to fit it."
msgstr "Putim wanpela PDF piksa long baksait bilong olgeta section\n"
"heading (\\s, \\s1, \\s2). Yusim Select... long\n"
"makim, na Scale/Shift long mekim i fit."

#: temp.glade:31788 temp.glade:31998
msgid "Dynamic Border"
msgstr "Dainamik Border"

#: temp.glade:31792
msgid "Draw a box around each section heading\n"
"that grows with the heading. Its look is\n"
"set by the cat:headingsbox|esb style."
msgstr "Droim wanpela box raunim olgeta section heading\n"
"na i kamap bikpela wantaim heading. Pasin bilong en\n"
"i stap long cat:headingsbox|esb style."

#: temp.glade:31816
msgid "If Section Headings sometimes extend to more \n"
"than one line, then a static PDF section heading\n"
"is unlikely to work. Instead, a dynamically\n"
"generated decorative section heading needs to\n"
"be set up to grow/shrink with the content of\n"
"the heading. Use this link to show the special\n"
"style, which needs to be enabled and defined."
msgstr "Sapos Hedin bilong Sekson i stap long mobeta olsem wanpela lain tasol, wanpela PDF hedin i no inap wok gut. Orait, yu mas redim wanpela dekoretiv hedin bilong sekson i ken kamap bikpela o liklik long wanem hedin i gat. Klikim dispela link long soim spesol stail, na yu mas opim na makim stail."

#: temp.glade:31854
msgid "Section Headings"
msgstr "Hedin bilong Sekson"

#: temp.glade:31859
msgid "Section Headings may be adorned with\n"
"a special graphic. Ensure that there is\n"
"adequate space - both horizontal as well\n"
"as vertical to make sure all headings fit."
msgstr "Ol Hedin bilong Sekson i ken gat wanpela spesol piksa.\n"
"Makim gut olsem i gat inap ples - long sait na long antap\n"
"na daunbilo - na olgeta hedin i ken pas gut."

#: temp.glade:31917
msgid "Full page"
msgstr "Olgeta pes"

#: temp.glade:31922
msgid "If set, the border is expanded to the full page. Otherwise it is expanded only to the gutter margins."
msgstr "Sapos i makim, border i ken go long olgeta pes. Sapos i no makim, em i go long gutter margin tasol."

#: temp.glade:31959
msgid "Click to edit the properties of the\n"
"Text Border (which is controlled by\n"
"the \\textborder style on the Styles tab)."
msgstr "Klikim long senisim ol propeti bilong\n"
"Text Border (stail \\textborder long\n"
"tab Styles i save kontrolim)."

#: temp.glade:31979
msgid "Use an existing PDF Border for the\n"
"entire publication."
msgstr "Usim wanpela PDF Border i stap pinis\n"
"long olgeta buk."

#: temp.glade:32002
msgid "Place a decorative border only around \n"
"the Scripture text (excludes introductions, \n"
"footnotes and other peripheral material)."
msgstr "Putim wanpela dekoretiv border long\n"
"Skripsa tekst tasol (i no gat ol introdaksen,\n"
"futnot na narapela ol samting i stap arasait)."

#: temp.glade:32021
msgid "Page Border"
msgstr "Pes Border"

#: temp.glade:32026
msgid "Place a uniform-sized decorative border\n"
"on every page regardless of content."
msgstr "Putim wanpela dekoretiv border i gat wankain\n"
"bikpela long olgeta pes, maski wanem samting i stap long en."

#: temp.glade:32050
msgid "Click to edit the properties of the\n"
"Page Border (which is controlled by\n"
"the \\pageborder style on the Styles tab)."
msgstr "Klikim long senisim ol propeti bilong\n"
"Pes Border (stail \\pageborder long\n"
"tab Styles i save kontrolim)."

#: temp.glade:32097
msgid "There are different kinds of borders that\n"
"can be applied to the publication. \n"
"\n"
"Note that if you use a border, it is likely\n"
"that you will need to adjust the margins\n"
"to make it fit."
msgstr "I gat narapela narapela kain border\n"
"i ken go long buk.\n"
"\n"
"Sapos yu usim border, yu mas senisim\n"
"ol margin long mekim i pas gut."

#: temp.glade:32208
msgid "End of Book Decoration"
msgstr "Dekoresen long Pinis bilong Buk"

#: temp.glade:32213
msgid "The end of each book may be adorned \n"
"with a special graphic."
msgstr "Long pinis bilong olgeta buk, yu ken putim\n"
"wanpela spesol piksa."

#: temp.glade:32252
msgid "End of Ayah"
msgstr "Pinis bilong Aya"

#: temp.glade:32257
msgid "Use the End of Ayah character in the\n"
"font to decorate the verse number."
msgstr "Usim kerekta Pinis bilong Aya long\n"
"font long dekoretim namba bilong ves."

#: temp.glade:32274
msgid "Verse Border Graphic"
msgstr "Piksa Border bilong Ves"

#: temp.glade:32279
msgid "Use a PDF graphic to decorate the verse \n"
"number. You may need to also adjust the\n"
"font properties to ensure the verse numbers\n"
"fit within the graphic."
msgstr "Usim wanpela PDF piksa long dekoretim namba\n"
"bilong ves. Maski yu mas senisim ol propeti\n"
"bilong font long ol namba bilong ves i pas\n"
"long insait bilong piksa."

#: temp.glade:32304
msgid "Click to edit the \\vp marker's properties on the Styles tab."
msgstr "Klikim long senisim ol seting bilong \\vp marker long Styles tab."

#: temp.glade:32355 temp.glade:32373
msgid "Vertical shift in pts of the verse decorator image.\n"
"  + values shift the decorator upwards\n"
"  - values shift the decorator downwards"
msgstr "Sip bilong piksa bilong dekoreta bilong ves long pts.\n"
"  + ol valu i kisim dekoreta i go antap\n"
"  - ol valu i kisim dekoreta i go daun"

#: temp.glade:32391
msgid "Scale verse decorator image. 1.0 = its own size,\n"
"0.5 = half size, 2.0 = double size."
msgstr "Senisim bikpela bilong piksa bilong verse decorator. 1.0 = sem bikpela bilong en yet,\n"
"0.5 = hap bikpela, 2.0 = tupela bikpela."

#: temp.glade:32422
msgid "Move Ayah"
msgstr "Mufim Aya"

#: temp.glade:32427
msgid "This option moves the Ayah\n"
"to the end of the verse. "
msgstr "Dispela opsen i mufim Aya\n"
"i go long pinis bilong ves. "

#: temp.glade:32448
msgid "Click to edit the \\v marker's properties on the Styles tab."
msgstr "Klikim long senisim ol propeti bilong \\v marker long tab Styles."

#: temp.glade:32478
msgid "Verse Number Decorator"
msgstr "Dekoreitim Namba bilong Ves"

#: temp.glade:32483
msgid "Verse numbers can be decorated using\n"
"either of the options shown below."
msgstr "Yu ken dekoreitim ol namba bilong ves\n"
"long wanpela bilong ol opsen i stap aninit."

#: temp.glade:32535
msgid "Adjust the styling of the dynamic \n"
"borders around book titles."
msgstr "Senisim stail bilong ol dainamik\n"
"bording raun long ol taitol bilong buk."

#: temp.glade:32570
msgid "Book Title Borders"
msgstr "Bording bilong Taitol bilong Buk"

#: temp.glade:32575
msgid "Dynamic borders can be applied to\n"
"book titles (\\mt1 and \\mt2). Styling\n"
"can be adjusted using the link below."
msgstr "Yu ken putim ol dainamik bording long\n"
"ol taitol bilong buk (\\mt1 na \\mt2). Yu ken\n"
"senisim stail long linga i stap aninit."

#: temp.glade:32596
msgid "Ornamental Decorations"
